  "steps": [
    "In a large bowl, mix the beef mince, grated onion, minced garlic, chopped parsley, cumin, paprika, ground coriander, cinnamon, black pepper and salt until evenly combined. Shape the mixture into 16 small meatballs.",
    "Heat the olive oil in a large deep frying pan or wide saucepan over medium heat. Add the sliced onion and cook for 5 minutes until softened and starting to turn golden. Add the sliced garlic and cook for 1 minute more.",
    "Stir in the canned tomatoes, tomato paste, water, cumin, paprika, chilli powder, salt and black pepper. Bring to a gentle simmer and cook for 10 minutes, stirring now and then, until the sauce thickens slightly.",
    "Nestle the meatballs into the sauce in a single layer. Cover and simmer gently for 12 to 15 minutes, turning the meatballs once, until cooked through and no longer pink in the centre.",
    "Use a spoon to make 4 small wells in the sauce. Crack an egg into each well, cover again, and cook for 5 to 7 minutes until the whites are set but the yolks are still soft, or longer if you prefer firmer yolks.",
    "Scatter with the remaining parsley and serve hot, ideally with bread or couscous if you like."
  ],
